# Build context hygiene. Everything here either bloats the image, breaks the build, or must never
# leave the machine.

# Secrets. First for a reason: .env holds BRIGHTDATA_API_KEY and the database password, and a
# COPY that swept it into a layer would bake both into the image permanently.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Reinstalled inside the container against the lockfile. Copying a host install also copies its
# platform-specific binaries, which is how a Windows build produces a container that cannot start.
**/node_modules

# Build output — regenerated in the build stage. Copying it in risks shipping a stale dist that
# silently disagrees with the sources beside it.
**/dist
**/.next
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Not needed at runtime.
**/test
**/.logs
**/.scratch
apps/web
apps/chaos-lab
docs
supabase
.git
.github
*.md
!README.md
